---
source: src/mcp/tools.rs
expression: PROXY_HTTP_DESCRIPTION
---
Make an HTTP request through a preset. The preset selects the base URL and authentication; you supply `path`, `method`, and optional `body` / `query`. Allow-listed methods and paths are validated server-side BEFORE any credential is injected. Sensitive presets trigger a desktop / TUI approval prompt; you cannot bypass approval. If the user previously approved a time-boxed window for this preset+action, the call proceeds without a new prompt and is recorded as 'windowed' in the audit log. Every call is recorded to a local audit log.
